-- title:
--   The local-expert estimate for either kind of passing probe.
-- statement:
--   The local-expert estimate for either kind of passing probe. The high-surplus branch
--   uses the common top band of the quantile construction; its raw mass is at least 1/32.
--   The labels are multiplied by the hidden sign, so correct feedback is represented by one.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.PriceGame.Charging.exists_probe_test`.
